{
  "annotation": "Single AI source annotator, not expert-certified; source pages inspected/rendered before any new-project inference. Hough circles assisted coordinates only, no learned detection. Scored ROIs include all visible semantic glyphs under valve/instrument/pump/inlet-outlet convention. Pipe size reducers, rock-trap transparent fitting, disconnected equipment-name oval, meter support bracket are explicit ignore regions, not negatives; text/line IDs are not equipment. Motors are visible instrument bubbles; compound square-with-circle panels are one glyph. Adjacency stops at intermediate semantic equipment. Unmarked four-arm pipe crossings remain separate. Edges may traverse outside ROI where the full source unambiguously shows a common header (Winnipeg2 downstream valves). Branch/dashed subsets overlap and are not independent samples. Extension applies the same semantic classes, including tank bodies, spray endpoints, instrument bubbles and complete off-page markers. Motors separate from the tank/pump body. Clarifier effluent pipes enter the collection tank separately, with no direct adjacency across the intermediate tank; branch cliques stop at semantic equipment. Truck and hose-reel pictograms, pipe reducers and disconnected equipment-name ovals are explicitly outside this target ontology. All visible target glyphs in each stated ROI are labeled, no post-inference exclusions.",
  "exposure": "The four whole pages and original35 labels were evaluated in v9. In v10 the original35 labels are development preservation data. Expanded labels were made from source-only crops while development localization/routing on the old ROIs ran; candidate output outside old ROIs was not inspected by annotation. Extension labels are withheld from selection, but whole-image and project exposure exists. Do not call this new-project/first-ever image-blind testing. None of these pages was used for gradient training.",
  "rights": "Government hosting does not imply redistribution rights. Source/crops/overlays/full OCR stay private ignored storage. Only normalized annotation, scores and original charts go to Git.",
